Title: Take Me Home, Country Roads
Artist: John Denver
Key: A major
Tempo: 82
Time: 4/4

# Four chords, one bar each, and verse and chorus are harmonically distinct —
# which is what makes this the one song in the corpus where the form score has
# something real to be wrong about.
#
# Note: the recording's beat grid is the worst in the corpus, and this chart is
# written in the song's bars rather than the tracker's. The tracker reads it at
# 0.53 confidence, emits 3.52 beats to the bar before the repair, and runs at
# 167 bpm — an *octave* above the 82 this song is in — so its bars are half bars
# and its chart comes out about twice as long as this one. The measured harmonic
# unit says the same thing from the other direction: the chords last 8 of the
# tracker's beats, which is two of its bars and one of the song's. A 2:1 bar
# ratio on this song is that octave and nothing else; it belongs to
# bench/run_bench.py's sync gate rather than to this grade.

